[
  {
    "sha": "9998a1c826ae4c4dc3a8dc0d79f63099563fe7d3",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDk5OThhMWM4MjZhZTRjNGRjM2E4ZGMwZDc5ZjYzMDk5NTYzZmU3ZDM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T22:34:10Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T22:34:10Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(motion): equal depth steps as an opt-in ladder parameter\n\nThe depth ladder keeps the remainder in the last step by default (top 20,\nbottom 2, stepdown 5 cuts 15, 10, 5, 2). The new `equal_steps` field of\n`links.approach` cuts the same number of levels in equal steps (15.5, 11,\n6.5, 2). The default does not change, so no posted G-code moves.\n\n- motion: `machining2d::equal_stepdown`, `ladder_stepdown` and\n  `cut_levels_for` give the stepdown of the mode to the one level law.\n  Pocket, adaptive, contour, slot, bore, circular and the 3-D pocket\n  ladders call `cut_levels_for`.\n- app: the approach DTO writes `equal_steps` only when on; the params\n  digest takes a byte only when on; the pocket region law reads the same\n  mode through `OpParams::ladder_stepdown`.\n- ui: one row, \"Equal depth steps\", in the Linking group of the Lead in /\n  Lead out tab.\n- docs/decisions/2012-equal-steps.md records the decision. Face, Trace,\n  Engrave and Trochoidal Slot have no links object: follow-up #2832.\n\nFixes #2012\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
